## F4 — Function-level access control (HIGH, always-on)

**OWASP:** A01:2025 · **CWE:** CWE-284 · **ASVS:** v5.0.0-8.2.1 · **Retest:** Restricted role blocked on direct route/API access (403 or redirect)

### MUST

- Enforce route/module access in `+layout.server.ts`, hooks, or BFF — not UI hide-only
- Redirect or error when user lacks permission on direct navigation
- BFF permission check before proxying admin operations

### MUST NOT

- Hide nav links as the only access control
- Trust client-side role checks without server enforcement

### Required tests

- Restricted role navigates directly to admin URL → blocked server-side

---

## F8 — Object-level authorization (HIGH, always-on)

**OWASP:** A01:2025 · **API:** API1:2023 · **CWE:** CWE-639 · **ASVS:** v5.0.0-8.2.2 · **Retest:** User A opens User B’s record URL → server load or BFF returns 403 or 404

The caller has the same role as the owner.

### MUST

- Server load, hook, or BFF authorizes that `{id}` before rendering or proxying
- The client treats 403 and 404 as not-found for the caller

### MUST NOT

- Decide ownership from an id in the route after the client has already rendered another user’s data
- Hide the link and still load the record

### Required tests

- Same-role user navigates directly to another user’s URL → blocked server-side

---

## F5 — Exposed API Calls (LOW)

**OWASP:** A path visible in the Network tab is informational. A route without auth or authz is **F4 / A01:2025**, not this finding. **CWE:** CWE-200 · **Retest:** Sensitive identifiers are in body or headers. Auth and admin paths are rate limited.

### MUST

- Record a missing auth or authz check as F4
- Put sensitive identifiers in body/headers — not URL query strings
- Rate limiting on auth and admin paths (edge or BFF)

### Accept

- SPA Network tab visibility is **normal** — guardrail is protect endpoints, not hide URLs

### Required tests

- New client-visible routes require an authenticated server load or a protected API (a miss is F4)
- New endpoints keep sensitive params out of the query string

---

## F7 — Cookies Without HttpOnly (LOW)

**OWASP:** A02:2025 · **CWE:** CWE-1004 · **Retest:** Session cookies show HttpOnly + Secure in DevTools

A missing flag on an auth or refresh cookie is exploitable: treat that miss as a merge blocker.

### MUST

- App-set session/auth cookies: `httpOnly: true`, `secure: true` (prod), `sameSite: 'lax'` or `'strict'`
- Review IdP and ingress cookie settings with DevOps in deployment checklist

### MUST NOT

- Set auth tokens via `document.cookie` when an HttpOnly cookie is the session mechanism
- Ship cookie setters missing any of the three flags

### Required checks

- DevTools → Application → Cookies: verify flags before VAPT

---

## F3 — File Upload UI (MEDIUM)

**OWASP:** A06:2025, A05:2025 · **CWE:** CWE-434 · **Retest:** Server rejects renamed wrong-type file (400)

### MUST

- Client upload UI calls a server endpoint with proper auth headers
- Show a user-facing error when the server rejects the file

### MUST NOT

- Rely on HTML `accept` attributes or client filename checks as sole validation
- Implement upload without matching server-side content validation (Tika + structure parse, generated storage name, decompression limit, production virus scan)

### Required tests

- Renamed wrong-type file rejected by server before processing

---

## Retest summary (Web app)

| Finding | Gate | Pass criteria |
|---------|------|---------------|
| F4 | Always-on, Critical if applicable | Restricted role blocked on direct route/API access |
| F8 | Always-on, Critical if applicable | Same-role user blocked on another user’s URL |
| F1 | Regression, High | User B everywhere after User A logout + User B login; access token not in web storage |
| F2 | Regression, Medium | No config leak endpoints; no RBAC/internal URLs in prod bundle |
| F3 | Regression, Medium | Server rejects invalid uploads (client UI is supplemental) |
| F5 | Regression, Low | Sensitive params not in the query string. Missing authz is F4 |
| F7 | Regression, Low; blocker if an auth cookie lacks flags | Session cookies HttpOnly + Secure |
| F6 | Regression, Low | Session policy confirmed with the API |
